feat(github-app): Cloudflare Worker webhook receiver

The missing piece that makes Port Daddy Fleet actually react to GitHub events. PR #146 ships the App auth + post-as primitive but no receiver — without this, the App can post but not react. Worker verifies HMAC-SHA256 signature with constant-time compare, builds a normalized envelope {event, delivery, channel: github:webhook:<event>, action, repository, installation_id, sender, payload}, forwards to operator's daemon via fetch. 22 vitest tests pass (signature pass/fail/missing/wrong-prefix, envelope normalization, forward success/non-2xx/network error, all Worker status-code branches). End-to-end smoke test verified live: valid HMAC -> 204 + daemon receives envelope; tampered HMAC -> 401 + no forward.


